Some stupid Retief-ripoff science fiction novel
I just read had the protagonist landing on a
planet with a near-ultraviolet sun, who then
puts on some sun screen with Skin Protection
Factor 1,000,000; some sort of nanobot lotion.

So, couldn't NetHack do something useful with a Skin
Protection Factor in either a grease can or a potion
jar (like potions of oil), that decayed slowly after
being applied, and gave, say, one AC improvement per
power of ten of SPF, decaying slowly at first, fast
at the end?

The grease can as a container would be especially nice,
making for a rare, much more valuable object resembling
a can of grease.

Just going a little nuts again, but the idea of
protection that wears away over time seems nice, since,\
once identified, there'd be this big "use it now, or
wait" issue to heighten self-criticism for overwaiting:
"YASD: SPF still in the jar".

